<title>USA: EG&amp;G says '97 EPS could be hurt by $0.10/shr.</title>
<headline>EG&amp;G says '97 EPS could be hurt by $0.10/shr.</headline>
<dateline>WELLESLEY, Mass. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>EG&amp;G Inc said Monday that continued production problems and other disruptions could hurt results the rest of the year, possibly reducing 1997 earnings by $0.10 per share.</p>
<p>The company said it had a series of production problems within its optoelectronics business segment in its first quarter and production problems at a micromachined sensor plant in Santa Clara, Calif.</p>
